# EchLub Multitask Governance

## Activation boundary

Writing any of the following inside an ordinary prompt does **not** prove Multitask activation:

```text
use Multitask
run tasks in parallel
launch async subagents
```

A work package requiring Cursor Multitask must declare an external launch precondition:

```text
Start from the Cursor Agents Window using /multitask
```

or:

```text
Create a Plan and choose Build in Parallel
```

The final report must record which Cursor surface was used.

## Dispatch-before-wait

For independent subagents:

```text
dispatch A
dispatch B
dispatch C
then await all
```

Forbidden:

```text
dispatch A
wait A
dispatch B
wait B
```

## Dependency rule

Only genuinely independent work may run concurrently.

Auditors depending on completed implementation or evidence run **after** those dependencies, not beside them.

## Agent catalog lifecycle

A work package must not:

```text
create a custom agent
and rely on that new agent in the same existing chat
```

After adding or changing `.cursor/agents/**`:

1. commit or preserve the changes;
2. reload the Cursor window;
3. open a fresh chat;
4. then invoke the custom agent.

## Runtime model verification

Frontmatter records the **requested** model, not proof of actual runtime routing.

A model-routing PASS requires runtime or request metadata identifying the actual model.

Agent prose claiming “I am Grok” is not proof.

## Failure classifications

Use:

```text
MULTITASK_NOT_ACTIVATED
TASK_TOOL_UNAVAILABLE
CUSTOM_AGENT_NOT_DISCOVERED
GROK_MODEL_UNAVAILABLE
GROK_MODEL_MISMATCH
MODEL_IDENTITY_UNVERIFIABLE
BACKGROUND_EXECUTION_BLOCKING
PARENT_CHOSE_SERIAL_EXECUTION
SUBAGENT_START_FAILED
```

## Model budget

The probe may use:

* one Grok custom subagent;
* two Composer smoke readers;
* one parent coordinator.

No API-backed model or automatic premium fallback is authorized.
